{
  "id": "ds087",
  "snapshot": "data_science",
  "instruction": "Using Jupyter Notebook, create a new notebook named `pres_influence_summary.ipynb` under `/home/user/analysis_results/`. The dataset `european_turnout.csv` is already available in that folder. In the notebook, load the dataset using pandas. Split the data into two groups based on the column `pres_more` (TRUE/FALSE). For each group, compute: (1) the average `euro_turnout`, (2) the average `nat_turnout`, and (3) the average turnout gap defined as (`nat_turnout - euro_turnout`). Save the summarized results as `pres_influence_summary.csv` with columns: `pres_more, avg_euro_turnout, avg_nat_turnout, avg_turnout_gap`, rounding all numeric values to two decimals.",
  "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/plotly/datasets/refs/heads/master/european_turnout.csv",

